  "story_id": "S091",
  "title": "Rbfox1 loss selectively represses a thalamic and midbrain axon-excitability module",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Rbfox1 loss produced its strongest mRNA responses in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut and 155 MB Glut, with a shared down-regulated core of Adgrb1, Nat8l, Dync1i2, Kcnc3, and Adss and a broader thalamic module containing Grin1, Vamp1, Scn1a, Scn1b, Kcnc3, Cntnap1, and Adgrb1.",
  "biological_interpretation": "RBFOX1 loss depresses mature axonal and synaptic excitability transcripts in a selective subset of neurons, making these genes better abundance readouts than a generic splicing-factor score.",
